From: Llaminar native graph progress repair
Subject: [PATCH] Prove finite-work eligibility before collapsing parallel graphs

The release's barrier-ROI heuristic treats waits, callbacks and child graphs
as one finite unit of work. A small graph can then put a wait before the
producer it expects to run on another branch, on the same in-order queue.
The graph's declared partial order is insufficient to estimate the duration
of these operations. Reject collapse for those typed nodes, including both
batch-memory wait widths; retain the existing ROI decision for finite compute,
copies and write-only batches. No environment override, larger queue limit,
extra event, host wait or alternate graph execution path is introduced.

Pinned base: ROCm/rocm-systems 6b0e43f341195e203754e08f850e437ff2fc09f9
             (therock-10.0, ROCm Core SDK 10.0.0)
Regression: V2_Integration_HIPGraphWaitConcurrency (flat/child, 32/64-bit)

diff --git a/hipamd/src/hip_graph_internal.cpp b/hipamd/src/hip_graph_internal.cpp
--- a/hipamd/src/hip_graph_internal.cpp
+++ b/hipamd/src/hip_graph_internal.cpp
@@ -1445,5 +1445,32 @@ bool GraphExecSegmented::ShouldCollapseToSingleStream() const {
   for (const auto& seg : segments_) {
     if (seg.dev_id != dev0) return false;
+    // The ROI model assumes finite, non-blocking work. A wait can require
+    // progress from another branch; putting both on one FIFO changes semantics
+    // and may deadlock. Child graphs/callbacks are opaque to this cost model.
+    // Keep their declared parallel streams rather than guessing a finite cost.
+    for (Node node : seg.nodes) {
+      switch (node->GetType()) {
+        case hipGraphNodeTypeGraph:
+        case hipGraphNodeTypeHost:
+        case hipGraphNodeTypeWaitEvent:
+        case hipGraphNodeTypeExtSemaphoreWait:
+          return false;
+        case hipGraphNodeTypeBatchMemOp: {
+          hipBatchMemOpNodeParams params{};
+          static_cast<hipGraphBatchMemOpNode*>(node)->GetParams(&params);
+          for (unsigned int i = 0; i < params.count; ++i) {
+            const auto operation = params.paramArray[i].operation;
+            if (operation == hipStreamMemOpWaitValue32 ||
+                operation == hipStreamMemOpWaitValue64) {
+              return false;
+            }
+          }
+          break;
+        }
+        default:
+          break;
+      }
+    }
   }

   size_t machine_threads = 0;

